Package: gpu-game-guard
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: games
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9)
Recommends: python3-pyqt5, zenity | kdialog | libnotify-bin, docker.io | podman
Suggests: polkitd | policykit-1
Homepage: https://github.com/darkiris4/gpu-game-guard
Description: ask before a game starts while GPU workloads are running
 GPU Game Guard watches for a game launch. When GPU containers or other
 GPU-hungry services are running, it pauses the launch, asks what to do,
 stops the workloads on request, starts the game again, and later offers to
 start the workloads again.
 .
 It manages Docker and Podman containers automatically and can also manage
 systemd services, commands and processes that are configured as targets.
 A settings window and a system tray icon need python3-pyqt5; without it the
 command line and the zenity, kdialog or notification dialogs still work.
 .
 The program runs as a systemd user service that is enabled for every user.
